# 📊 Segment Tree + Fenwick Tree (BIT) Master Sheet — Advanced DS

These are **advanced range query data structures** used when:

* arrays are dynamic (updates happen)
* and we need fast range queries

---

# 0. When to Use These?

```text id="st0"
Ask:

✔ Need range sum / min / max queries?
✔ Need updates + queries both?
✔ Prefix sum is not enough (because updates happen)?
✔ Need O(log n) instead of O(n)?
```

If YES → Segment Tree or BIT.

---

# 1. Segment Tree vs BIT (Fenwick)

| Feature     | Segment Tree      | BIT            |
| ----------- | ----------------- | -------------- |
| Ease        | Medium-Hard       | Easy-Medium    |
| Operations  | Any (min/max/sum) | Mostly sum/XOR |
| Flexibility | Very high         | Limited        |
| Memory      | O(4n)             | O(n)           |
| Speed       | O(log n)          | O(log n)       |

